where __MATH_1__ is the distance from the origin and __MATH_2__ is the cross-radial component of the instantaneous velocity (i.e. the component perpendicular to the position vector), which by convention is positive for counter-clockwise motion and negative for clockwise motion.

Therefore, the instantaneous angular acceleration ''α'' of the particle is given by

